# Canonical authorship.
#
# This repository has one living contributor. Commits had landed under agent-run
# identities, under a malformed noreply address git never validated, under
# GitHub's web-UI committer, and under two further personal addresses. None of
# them was a separate person.
#
# The history was REWRITTEN on 2026-08-17 (`git filter-repo --mailmap`, this
# file) so every commit's author and committer is the identity below, and every
# agent co-author trailer is gone. Commit hashes therefore changed and `origin`
# was force-pushed; the pre-rewrite object graph is preserved at
# `~/.cache/kinu-handoff/pre-rewrite-all-refs.bundle`.
#
# Every commit reachable from `main` is already the canonical identity, so the
# rows below are the declaration a future commit made from a different machine
# or a web edit is measured against. The agent-run addresses that predate the
# rename are deliberately absent: they name no living identity, they occur only
# on local `archive/*` tags, and nothing will ever author under them again.

